W: 1. A Highland lad my love was born,
W: The Lawland laws he held in scorn;
W: But he still was faithful to his clan,
W: My gallant braw John Highlandman.
W:
W: (Chorus:)
W: Sing hey, my braw John Highlandman,
W: Sing ho, my braw John Highlandman;
W: There's no' a lad in a' the lan'
W: Was match wi' my John Highlandman.
W:
W: 2. With his philabeg[1] and tartan plaid,
W: And gude claymore[2] down by his side;
W: The ladies' hearts he did trepan
W: My gallant braw John Highlandman.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 3.They banish'd him beyond the sea;
W: But ere the bud was on the tree,
W: Adoun my cheeks the pearls they ran,
W: Embracing my John Highlandman.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W:
W: [1] philsbeg: kilt
W: [2] claymore: two-handed sword
%
